---
// DRAFT terms of use (CONTENT.md "Legal"). Must be reviewed by a lawyer before launch.
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use | Lighthouse Maritime Agency"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the Lighthouse Maritime Agency website."
  heading="Terms of use"
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by {SITE.legalName} ({SITE.rc}), {SITE.address.short}, Nigeria. By using it you accept
    these terms. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on this site</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the information on this site accurate, but it is provided for general information only.
    The port call guide in particular describes how port calls usually work in Nigeria; requirements can
    change, so confirm them with our operations desk before your vessel arrives.
  </p>

  <h2>Estimates and services</h2>
  <p>
    A PDA request sent through this site is a request for an estimate, not a contract. Any services we provide
    are governed by the agreement made with you for that port call.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not misuse the site, try to gain unauthorised access to it, or interfere with how it works.</li>
    <li>Do not send false, unlawful or harmful content through our forms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The content, design and logo on this site belong to {SITE.legalName} or its licensors. You may view and
    print pages for your own use, but not copy or reuse them for any other purpose without our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>We are not responsible for the content of other websites we link to, such as Google Maps.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss arising from your use of, or reliance on,
    information on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>How we handle your personal data is explained in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.admin.email}`}>{SITE.admin.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
